# PART 13 — SQLMap Common Problems

## `no column(s) found`

Example:

```text
[WARNING] no column(s) found
```

Meaning:

> SQLMap table ke column names retrieve nahi kar pa raha.

Try:

```bash
--columns
```

THM lab mein SQLMap common column existence check bhi suggest kar sakta hai.

---

## `--no-cast`

SQLMap kabhi-kabhi suggest kar sakta hai:

```bash
--no-cast
```

Ye SQLMap ke casting behavior ko change karta hai.

---

## `--hex`

SQLMap data ko hexadecimal representation ke through retrieve karne ki koshish kar sakta hai:

```bash
--hex
```

Ye normal first-choice flag nahi hai; problem aane par SQLMap suggest kar sakta hai.

